##DESCRIPTION
##  Algebra problem: true or false for inequality
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('algebra', 'inequality', 'fraction')

## DBsubject('Basic Math')
## DBchapter('Rates')
## DBsection('Rates')
## Date('11/11/2015')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");

$mph      = random(15, 90, 15);
$ftpersec = $mph * 5280 / 3600;

BEGIN_PGML
Convert the following: [$ftpersec] feet/sec is [_]{$mph} miles per hour.

Recall that 1 mile is 5280 feet, 60 seconds is 1 minute and 60 minutes is 1 hour.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
We start with the given information and then multiply by factors that equal 1 due to unit conversions:

[```
[$ftpersec] \frac{\text{feet}}{\text{sec}} \times 
\frac{1~\text{mile}}{5280~\text{feet}} \times
\frac{60~\text{sec}}{1~\text{min}} \times 
\frac{60~\text{min}}{1~\text{hour}} 
= [$mph] \frac{\text{mi}}{\text{hour}}
```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
